---
title: Pear Cake with Pine Nuts
servings: 8
rating: 5
source.name: MyRecipes.com
source.url: http://www.myrecipes.com/recipe/pear-cake-with-pine-nuts-10000000226688/
tags: Desserts
---

Preheat oven to 350°F.

Lightly spoon @all-purpose flour{1 1/4%cups} into dry measuring cups, and level with a knife.
Combine flour, @sugar{3/4%cup}, and @salt{1/8%tsp} in a #large bowl{}; stir well with a whisk.

Cut in @butter{1/4%cup}(chilled, cut into small pieces) with a pastry blender or 2 knives
until mixture resembles coarse meal.

Remove 1/3 cup flour mixture; place in a #small bowl{}.
Stir in @pine nuts{2%tbsp}(toasted) and @ground cinnamon{1/4%tsp}; set aside.

In a #large bowl{}, combine the remaining flour mixture, @sour cream{1/3%cup}(fat-free),
@milk{1/4%cup}(1% low-fat), @lemon rind{1%tsp}(grated), @vanilla extract{1%tsp},
@baking powder{1/2%tsp}, @baking soda{1/4%tsp}, and @egg{1}(large).

Beat with a #mixer at medium speed until well blended.
Pour the batter into a #9-inch round cake pan{} coated with @cooking spray{}.

Arrange the @pear{2%cups}(peeled, cored, thinly sliced) evenly over the batter.
Sprinkle with pine nut mixture. 

Bake at 350°F for ~{45%minutes} or until a wooden pick inserted in center comes out clean;
cool completely on a wire rack.
